    <statement><p>Suppose <m>\vec v\cdot \vec w=7</m> and
<m>||\vec v\times\vec w|| = 3</m>, and the
angle between <m>\vec v</m> and <m>\vec w</m> is <m>\theta</m>.  Find</p>
<p><alert>(a)</alert>
<m>\tan\theta =</m> <fillin characters="45" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert>(b)</alert>
<m>\theta  =</m> <fillin characters="45" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{3}{7}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\tan^{-1}\mathopen{}\left(\frac{3}{7}\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>(a)</alert>
Since <m>\vec v\cdot \vec w= ||\vec v||\,||\vec w||\cos \theta</m> and
<m>||\vec v\times\vec w||=||\vec v||\, ||\vec w||\sin\theta</m>,
<me>\tan \theta = \frac{\sin\theta}{\cos\theta} =
   \frac{||\vec v\times\vec w||}{\vec v\cdot \vec w} =
   \frac{3}{7} = 0.428571.</me>




<alert>(b)</alert>
Then <m>\theta = \tan^{-1}(0.428571) = 0.404892</m>.



</solution>
